# Authentication — session login required (all modules)

AML **session login is required** on `https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506` for **every** module. Agents must never treat login as bypassed and must never ask the user to re-enable it.

When Command Center or a module requires a session, sign in via `tests/helpers/aml-login.ts` using `.env` credentials (`EMAIL` / `PASSWORD`, aliases `AML_USERNAME` / `AML_PASSWORD`). Do **not** hard-code the password in specs, locators, agents, rules, or committed JSON.

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Default 2506 user | **QAUSER2** |
| Password | gitignored `.env` only (`PASSWORD` / `AML_PASSWORD`) |
| Login UI | Clari5 Command Center `/clari5-cc/login` (host root `/` may still show Apache) |
| Opt out of auto-login | `PW_SKIP_AML_LOGIN=1` (exception only — not the default) |

Missing `EMAIL` / `PASSWORD` when the login form is shown is a **live-UI blocker**. Other hosts (e.g. 2502) use that environment’s `.env` separately.

## Signed-in flows — always automate

Keep automating with an authenticated session: module navigation, TLS/HTTPS, masking/privacy, keyboard/WCAG, performance/SLA, layout, maker-checker, audit trail, and all other signed-in product flows. Session login is established by the fixture / `aml-login` helper — specs do not hard-code credentials.

## Negative / multi-role auth cases — Partial unless opted in

Do **not** generate, heal-back, or add scripts for these Excel cases unless the user asks **or** sets `QA_INCLUDE_AUTH_CASES=1`:

| Kind | Examples |
|------|----------|
| Unauthenticated access | Open a module URL with no session; expect sign-in / access denied |
| Login / session expiry | Redirect to login, session expiry, expired token |
| Unauthorized role | “Log in as a user without permission”, “unauthorized role cannot…” |
| Role-based access | “all authorized AML roles”, “role-based access”, RBAC / read-only auditor |

Put those Excel rows in **Partial** (`Partial - Authentication (automate only when QA_INCLUDE_AUTH_CASES=1)`). Normalize excludes them (`pipeline/scripts/nfr-auth-automation-scope.cjs`). List them in `blockedUiCaseIds` / `deferredCaseIds` with that reason. **Do not** use `test.skip()`.

**Never** label Automable as “login bypassed” — session login is always enabled.

## Include negative auth cases only when specified

Bring unauthenticated / expiry / unauthorized-role cases into Playwright **only** if the user asks **or** sets `QA_INCLUDE_AUTH_CASES=1`.

Applies to: `fsd-figma-pipeline` (Excel Automable), `qa-automation-pipeline`, generator, healer, execute-raise-defects, headed/headless executors.
